There are two files to demonstrate c assembly working together
a_gcd.s : Assembly for a gcd computation
main.c : C code that calls gcd

Compilation:
	gcc a_gcd.s main.c	

There is another c_gcd.c : C version of the above assembly.
	The idea is so that you can map variable names and registers


Do the following to see the code in the executable:
readelf -W -a a.out > ELF
In objdump -d a.out look for  gcd 
	See the code matching what is in a_gcd.s
	Notice how the jump address got determined
	Notice parameters and return value

In this ELF file  look for the info on gcd and main - should be in the same address
Also od -x a.out -N 20 -j <<address_of_gcd>>  a.out
	This will show the same code just in binary

Also do the following
gdb a.out     (clearly you cant find the c code because no -g given)
However you can do the following
(gdb) disass /r gcd			( the /r is to see the binary code)
Notice the code that we wrote for gcd
Notice the address is different!
